<title>UK: Readicut first-half profit nudges higher.</title>
<headline>Readicut first-half profit nudges higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.12		   vs *0.91</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.63		   vs same</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.3		    vs *2.8</p>
<p> Turnover		   127.6		  vs 112.7</p>
<p> Operating result	   4.7		  vs 4.8</p>
<p>NOTE - *Earnings per share in the previous year were 1.33 pence before an exceptional charge of 1.24 million stg. Pre-tax pre-exceptional profits last year totalled 4.0 million.</p>
<p>The British specialist textile group first-half results had been hit by poor performance of three of its businesses, which suffered losses due to restructuring or start-up costs. Gearing stands at 81 percent of shareholder funds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
